From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Editor UI fixes for native Wayland and XWayland (experimental carry)

Local work in progress, carried only under --with wayland_ui and only on a
development snapshot at or after o3de/o3de 0af429a2ea (the merge of #20204).
Sixteen commits squashed into one diff; none has been proposed upstream yet.

- AzQtComponents: the window manager moves the Editor window (tile snapping),
  no second title bar on Wayland, window moves requested with the true pointer
  position on X11, floating windows can be minimized and maximized on X11.
- Editor viewport: native surface handling so the layout, level load and game
  mode work on Wayland.
- Camera look in the Editor viewport on Wayland.
- Vulkan RHI: follow a window whose wl_surface was replaced (Particle Editor
  crash), create the surface on the connection the wl_surface belongs to
  (Material Editor and the other standalone tools).
- Docking: floating panels can be moved and docked on Wayland and under
  XWayland; drop zone overlay and drag ghost fixes.
- ViewportUi: viewport controls stay over the viewport on Wayland.

Known gaps: docking a floating panel into another floating panel; on GNOME
the dragged window does not follow the pointer during a docking drag, so the
panel's tab docks and the rest of its title bar moves.

---
diff --git a/Code/Editor/CryEdit.cpp b/Code/Editor/CryEdit.cpp
index 88a56da8ab..fdb6a632b2 100644
--- a/Code/Editor/CryEdit.cpp
+++ b/Code/Editor/CryEdit.cpp
@@ -1552,6 +1552,17 @@ bool CCryEditApp::InitInstance()
 #endif
     mainWindowWrapper->setGuest(mainWindow);
 
+#if defined(Q_OS_LINUX)
+    // On Wayland the viewport keeps its ancestors non-native (see RenderViewportWidget). If the
+    // main window were turned native later, for example by a script asking for its window id, Qt
+    // would re-parent the viewport and destroy the surface the renderer is presenting to. Make
+    // it native now, before any viewport exists, so that later requests change nothing.
+    if (QGuiApplication::platformName() == QLatin1String("wayland"))
+    {
+        mainWindow->winId();
+    }
+#endif
+
     // Note: we should use getNativeHandle to get the HWND from the widget, but
     // it returns an invalid handle unless the widget has been shown and polished and even then
     // it sometimes returns an invalid handle.
